## Check that the enums in lib/builtins/cpu_model/x86.c, which fill
## __cpu_model/__cpu_features2, agree with llvm/TargetParser/X86TargetParser.def,
## from which clang takes the indices and bit positions it emits for
## __builtin_cpu_is, __builtin_cpu_supports and function multiversioning.
## See llvm/test/Other/x86-cpu-model-abi for the checker's own tests.

# RUN: %python %llvm_src/utils/check_x86_cpu_model_abi.py \
# RUN:   --def %llvm_src/include/llvm/TargetParser/X86TargetParser.def \
# RUN:   --x86-c %crt_src/lib/builtins/cpu_model/x86.c \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: OK: {{[0-9]+}} vendors, {{[0-9]+}} CPU types, {{[0-9]+}} CPU subtypes, {{[0-9]+}} features match
